{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Where is the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/532f5b028e1496476b61a44ef5012c2af4256251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = -2x^{3} + 18x + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"21\" /> increasing?\n</p><p><br />\n\t\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a347fb7915d6712c8859f2819485cabbe10558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\left( -\\dfrac{7}{4}, \\dfrac{7}{4} \\right)  \\quad \t\t\t\\textbf{(B) } (-\\infty, \\infty)  \\quad \t\t\t\\textbf{(C) } \\left(-\\sqrt{3}, \\sqrt{3}\\right)  \\quad \t\t\t\\textbf{(D) } \\left( -\\infty , -\\dfrac{7}{4} \\right) \\text{and} \\left( \\dfrac{7}{4}, \\infty \\right) \\quad \t\t\t\\textbf{(E) } \\left(-\\infty, -\\sqrt{3} \\right) \\text{and} \\left(\\sqrt{3}, \\infty\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"900\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is increasing whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fda8ebf5fdf3a5bb2fa21e33b032ec7019f62a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. Finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/8/d188734450a657d218a5d8bd9bf891edc4361743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x) = -6x^2 + 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" />, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd782cb3176ac649ee5ed90ed255989b9c89a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/4735d3c2a54dd480df84d86505ab9187b32e03f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\pm \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cfc32b0aa554c9d98af355dafe67283ad403820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"17\" /> is a quadratic and its leading coefficient is negative, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bbad379658bd32e9b6479bbd666b93a96e6b48ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is positive whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> lies between these roots, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is increasing for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c8f8c2438775a0a7ec8b1cbcfba379d29cf89bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\left(-\\sqrt{3}, \\sqrt{3}\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"175\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Cont